      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HOPEFUL (1) has the most persuasive recent form, having chased SIGIRIYA ROCK to a neck at Atherton before another solid third at Gordonvale when held up leaving the 300m. The top weight is the obvious impost, but his record around 2000m gives him the right platform to turn those placings into a win. HURRICANE ROSIE (5) has been close enough in two recent runs without quite landing the blow, and her good track record keeps her firmly in the main danger bracket. THE DRILLER (3) has not been sharp at his past two, yet the quick back-up, weight relief and strong record with Adam Sewell give him a credible rebound case. EAGLE WARRIOR (7) was better than the bare result at Bowen after racing wide early, and his proven record around this distance makes him the value runner among the selected chances.",
